WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.840
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 2: School and Learning.

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.120
Welcome to Unit 2!

3
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.760
This unit is all about school and learning.

4
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:16.080
You will talk about your lessons, your teacher, and
the subjects you study, like mathematics and grammar.

5
00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.040
You will learn the words for the supplies you
use every day, such as an eraser and your books.

6
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:27.860
You will find out how to get ready for a contest,
write a short report, and use the library well.

7
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.200
Best of all, you will learn to talk about things that
happened in the past — what you studied, where you went,

8
00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.840
and why you enjoyed it.

9
00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:41.660
By the end, you will be ready to cheer for
the Grammar Champions in this unit's story!

10
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:48.240
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:56.280
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name the people,
places, and supplies at school, using words like teacher,

12
00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:57.660
library, and eraser.

13
00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:02.700
you will also talk about your school
subjects, such as mathematics and grammar.

14
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:10.420
you will also tell about things that happened before,
using the simple past tense (studied, prepared, went).

15
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:13.380
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:21.820
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: teacher,
author, library, graduate, mathematics, grammar.

17
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:27.740
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:31.480
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.660
The reading sequence includes A Day at
School and Getting Ready for the Contest.

20
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:38.620
Read actively.

21
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:44.120
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

22
00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.060
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

23
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.400
The first language focus is The Simple Past Tense.

24
00:01:54.420 --> 00:02:01.380
We use the simple past tense to talk about things that
already happened — yesterday, last week, or a long time ago.

25
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:04.180
It helps us tell stories and say what we did.

26
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:10.940
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

27
00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:16.700
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Talk About Your School Day.

28
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:21.540
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

29
00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.740
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

30
00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:29.420
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

31
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:31.260
You are ready to begin.

32
00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:37.680
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

33
00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.660
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

34
00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:46.680
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
